iving effects to share consolidation in January 2025).","section":"Segment reporting","block":323,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-078731","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-07-16","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001769256","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1769256/000121390026078731/ea0296080-6k_xchange.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9846771389d4dc09595cbc77276b3e5be5a9694c952c131163f3e51ecdb6845e.bin","sha256":"9846771389d4dc09595cbc77276b3e5be5a9694c952c131163f3e51ecdb6845e"}},{"id":"42f0a94cbf2e66eabe07a61d72ff1e3ae7559776ab2c9fea6f04702eeb09a976","quote":"9. NOTES PAYABLE","context":"The 57,786 Class A ordinary shares (after giving effects to share consolidation in January 2025) are subject to a make-whole cash-settled provision, and 20,861 Class A ordinary shares (after giving effects to share consolidation in January 2025) of which are also subject to redemption. The Company assessed the redemption terms and assessed it is probable that the Company will redeem these ordinary shares. The 57,786 ordinary shares (after giving effects to share consolidation in January 2025) fall in the classification of a liability. As of September 30, 2025 and March 31, 2026, the Company recorded the liabilities of RMB 165,161 and RMB 160,034 in the account of “Contingent liabilities for payable for asset acquisition”. The change in the balance as of September 30, 2025 and March 31, 2026 arose from change in foreign exchange rates.","section":"Segment reporting","block":324,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-078731","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-07-16","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0001769256","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1769256/000121390026078731/ea0296080-6k_xchange.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/9846771389d4dc09595cbc77276b3e5be5a9694c952c131